ing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-c1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-c1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"c1-natural","name":"Cambridge English — Bank accounts (C1–C2)","levels":["C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/c1l062-bank-accounts","task":"Tabiiy nutqdagi maqsad va muhim shartlarni tinglab, qisqa xulosa yozing.","lesson":"en-c1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-c1-12-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Nominalisation: jarayon va bajaruvchi: Til vositasini tanlang: Implement → noun: ___","answers":["implementation"],"explanation":"Implement → implementation; decide → decision jarayonni noun qiladi. Nominalisation matnni ixcham bog‘laydi, ammo agent va vaqtni yashirishi mumkin. It led to the implementation of … o‘rniga kim nima qilganini yozish ba’zan aniqroq.","hint":"implementation / evaluation / allocation","options":["implementation","implement","implements"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Nominalisation: jarayon va bajaruvchi"},{"id":"en-c1-12-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Ellipsis va substitution: Til vositasini tanlang: Did so substitution qolipini to‘ldiring: They tested it, and we did ___ too.","answers":["so"],"explanation":"So/neither yordamchi bilan: So do I; neither did she. Do so oldingi amal, one/ones ot, so/not clause mazmunini almashtirishi mumkin. Ellipsis kontekstdan tiklanadigan qismni tashlaydi; turli vazifalarni noto‘g‘ri tenglashtirmang.","hint":"do so / one / I think so / neither did","options":["so","either","neither"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Ellipsis va substitution"},{"id":"en-c1-12-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Complex relative va noun clauses: Til vositasini tanlang: ___ matters is whether access improves.","answers":["What"],"explanation":"What = the thing that; the thing what standard shakl emas. Whoever shaxsni umumiy tanlaydi; whose egalikni, which oldingi clausega ishora qilishi mumkin. That-clause propositionni beradi; whether muqobil/noaniqlikni saqlaydi.","hint":"what matters / whether … / whoever … / which …","options":["What","When","Where"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Complex relative va noun clauses"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-c1-13','en-c1-13',null,5,13,'published',1,'{"id":"en-c1-13","baseId":"en-c1-13","revision":1,"level":"C1","levelIndex":5,"order":13,"title":"Cohesion: reference va lexical chains","objective":"Matn bo‘ylab fikr zanjirini pronoun, sinonim va aniq takror bilan saqlaysiz.","context":"Cohesion: reference va lexical chains","prerequisites":["en-c1-12"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin.","Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas.","Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang."],"pattern":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","examples":["Attendance rose, but this increase needs explanation.","Participation also depends on meaningful involvement.","The trial introduced a new timetable.","This intervention was reviewed after two weeks.","The timetable, rather than the survey, caused confusion.","Repeating the term can improve precision."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-c1-13-v0","term":"cohesion","meaning":"matn bog‘liqligi","ipa":"/kəʊˈhiːʒən/","collocation":"maintain cohesion","example":"maintain cohesion"},{"id":"en-c1-13-v1","term":"referent","meaning":"tayanch birlik","ipa":"/ˈrefərənt/","collocation":"resolve a referent","example":"resolve a referent"},{"id":"en-c1-13-v2","term":"engagement","meaning":"faol ishtirok","ipa":"/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒmənt/","collocation":"meaningful engagement","example":"A report says that attendance rose and then describes this as greater engagement."},{"id":"en-c1-13-v3","term":"precision","meaning":"aniqlik","ipa":"/prɪˈsɪʒən/","collocation":"lexical precision","example":"Repeating the term can improve precision."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","Attendance rose, but this increase needs explanation.","Participation also depends on meaningful involvement."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["Attendance and engagement are related but distinct.","Counts and interviews provide different evidence.","Use a precise reference chain for each construct."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"This intervention was reviewed after two weeks.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-13-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-c1-13-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: Attendance rose; this ___ needs explanation. (increase)","answers":["increase"],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["increase","increasing","increases"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Attendance rose; this ___ needs explanation. (increase)","answers":["increase"],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it"},{"id":"en-c1-13-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Attendance rose, but this increase needs explanation."],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","tokens":["Attendance","rose,","but","this","increase","needs","explanation."]},{"id":"en-c1-13-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Attendance rose, so meaningful engagement definitely rose.","answers":["Attendance rose, but meaningful engagement requires separate evidence."],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it"},{"id":"en-c1-13-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["matn bog‘liqligi","tayanch birlik","faol ishtirok","aniqlik"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","left":["cohesion","referent","engagement","precision"],"options":["matn bog‘liqligi","tayanch birlik","faol ishtirok","aniqlik"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Referentni oching: This caused confusion. (timetable nazarda)","answers":["The timetable caused confusion."],"hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin."},{"id":"en-c1-13-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["Attendance and engagement are related but distinct.","Counts and interviews provide different evidence.","Use a precise reference chain for each construct."],"answers":["Attendance and engagement are related but distinct.\nCounts and interviews provide different evidence.\nUse a precise reference chain for each construct."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"A report says that attendance rose and then describes this as greater engagement. The terms are related but not identical: being present does not show how actively someone participated. Later, “this caused confusion” could refer either to the timetable or to the survey mentioned in the previous sentence. The editor repeats the timetable explicitly and keeps attendance as the term for the measured count. She uses engagement only when discussing the separate interview evidence. Avoiding repetition is not worth introducing a different construct or an ambiguous pronoun. A cohesive text gives readers a reliable chain of ideas. That chain can include deliberate repetition, clear reference, and carefully chosen lexical variation rather than a different synonym in every sentence.","sentences":["A report says that attendance rose and then describes this as greater engagement.","The terms are related but not identical: being present does not show how actively someone participated.","Later, “this caused confusion” could refer either to the timetable or to the survey mentioned in the previous sentence.","The editor repeats the timetable explicitly and keeps attendance as the term for the measured count.","She uses engagement only when discussing the separate interview evidence.","Avoiding repetition is not worth introducing a different construct or an ambiguous pronoun.","A cohesive text gives readers a reliable chain of ideas.","That chain can include deliberate repetition, clear reference, and carefully chosen lexical variation rather than a different synonym in every sentence."],"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-13-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Attendance engagementga tengmi?","answers":["not necessarily"],"explanation":"Presence active contribution emas.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["not necessarily","always","neither can be measured"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Editor nega timetable takrorladi?","answers":["to resolve an ambiguous reference"],"explanation":"This qaysi obyektga noma’lum.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["to resolve an ambiguous reference","to hide the survey","to increase word count"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["A report says that attendance rose and then describes this as greater engagement.","The terms are related but not identical: being present does not show how actively someone participated.","Later, “this caused confusion” could refer either to the timetable or to the survey mentioned in the previous sentence.","The editor repeats the timetable explicitly and keeps attendance as the term for the measured count.","She uses engagement only when discussing the separate interview evidence.","Avoiding repetition is not worth introducing a different construct or an ambiguous pronoun.","A cohesive text gives readers a reliable chain of ideas.","That chain can include deliberate repetition, clear reference, and carefully chosen lexical variation rather than a different synonym in every sentence."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is cohesion. A report says that attendance rose and then describes this as greater engagement. The terms are related but not identical: being present does not show how actively someone participated. Speaker two: My main point is precision. Repeat a term when variation would change the measured concept. A report says that attendance rose and then describes this as greater engagement. The terms are related but not identical: being present does not show how actively someone participated. Later, “this caused confusion” could refer either to the timetable or to the survey mentioned in the previous sentence. The editor repeats the timetable explicitly and keeps attendance as the term for the measured count. She uses engagement only when discussing the separate interview evidence. Avoiding repetition is not worth introducing a different construct or an ambiguous pronoun. A cohesive text gives readers a reliable chain of ideas. That chain can include deliberate repetition, clear reference, and carefully chosen lexical variation rather than a different synonym in every sentence.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-13.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-13-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Attendance engagementga tengmi?","answers":["not necessarily"],"explanation":"Presence active contribution emas.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["not necessarily","always","neither can be measured"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Editor nega timetable takrorladi?","answers":["to resolve an ambiguous reference"],"explanation":"This qaysi obyektga noma’lum.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["to resolve an ambiguous reference","to hide the survey","to increase word count"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["cohesion","precision"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["This intervention was reviewed after two weeks."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-13-dictation.mp3","transcript":"This intervention was reviewed after two weeks."}]},"writing":{"task":"Reportda reference chain yarating; attendance va engagement uchun alohida dalil bering.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":420,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"Attendance increased during the trial. This increase refers to the number of people present, rather than the quality of their involvement. Interviews provide separate evidence of engagement, but they cover only a small group. The timetable caused confusion during the first week; naming it explicitly avoids an ambiguous “this.” In the revision, I retain key terms when a synonym would change the construct being measured. Cohesion should help readers follow precise ideas, not merely prevent repeated words.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["Attendance rose, but this increase needs explanation.","Participation also depends on meaningful involvement.","The trial introduced a new timetable."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Reportda reference chain yarating; attendance va engagement uchun alohida dalil bering. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":150,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Reportda reference chain yarating; attendance va engagement uchun alohida dalil bering.","exit":[[{"id":"en-c1-13-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Attendance rose; this ___ needs explanation. (increase)","answers":["increase"],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it"},{"id":"en-c1-13-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Participation depends ___ involvement.","answers":["on"],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it"},{"id":"en-c1-13-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"This intervention was ___ after two weeks. (review)","answers":["reviewed"],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it"},{"id":"en-c1-13-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Attendance engagementga tengmi?","answers":["not necessarily"],"explanation":"Presence active contribution emas.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["not necessarily","always","neither can be measured"]},{"id":"en-c1-13-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Editor nega timetable takrorladi?","answers":["to resolve an ambiguous reference"],"explanation":"This qaysi obyektga noma’lum.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","options":["to resolve an ambiguous reference","to hide the survey","to increase word count"]}],[{"id":"en-c1-13-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Participation also depends on meaningful involvement."],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","tokens":["Participation","also","depends","on","meaningful","involvement."]},{"id":"en-c1-13-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Participation depends ___ involvement.","answers":["on"],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it"},{"id":"en-c1-13-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["This intervention was reviewed after two weeks."],"explanation":"This/it/they referenti yaqin va aniq bo‘lsin. Sinonimni takror uchun ishlatish tushunchani o‘zgartirmasin: attendance participationga har doim teng emas. Topic chain va reference xaritasini tekshirib, muhim atamani kerak joyda takrorlang.","hint":"attendance → this increase / the intervention → it","tokens":["This","intervention","was